	(embedded_fonts no)
	(title_block
		(title "Frugal-IoT Irrigation - Lolin S2 Mini reference wiring")
		(date "2026-09-22")
		(rev "C")
		(comment 1 "Documentation only - not a PCB. See README.md.")
		(comment 2 "Pin assignments are fixed by [env:s2_mini] in platformio.ini.")
	)
	(text "1.  12 V INPUT AND PROTECTION"
		(at 20.32 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.2 3.2)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a1a8087a-56ac-4bb6-94b6-1da3cf951324")
	)
	(text "D1 is series reverse-polarity protection, costing ~0.4 V - a 12 V solenoid still operates"
		(at 20.32 73.66 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "83fefb3b-0d34-4536-a667-98087d040477")
	)
	(text "at 11.6 V. F1 protects the BATTERY, not the board: a shorted valve cable across a"
		(at 20.32 76.66 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "1bfa77cb-e6bc-4f4d-81bf-55db29f14405")
	)
	(text "lead-acid bank is a fire risk and nothing else here limits that current."
		(at 20.32 79.66 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c23cfb0d-0b9c-400e-9e38-2f7d9cf1a2d3")
	)
	(text "2.  5 V SUPPLY"
		(at 20.32 96.52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.2 3.2)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "967be67a-9a36-4493-9af0-53951e01f8cb")
	)
	(text "D2 IS NOT OPTIONAL, and the buck setting is part of it. The S2 Mini ties VBUS straight to"
		(at 20.32 147.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "deacb916-987a-4402-84bc-f8cb65f4503c")
	)
	(text "USB 5 V, so both supplies meet on one node the moment someone plugs in to flash the board."
		(at 20.32 150.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "876e2813-bb2d-4995-a29c-e334c3eaf2af")
	)
	(text "Set the buck to 5.2 V: after D2 the rail is ~4.9 V, just BELOW USB, so when USB is present"
		(at 20.32 153.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "8c13374a-ffef-474e-870c-f04be407f82d")
	)
	(text "it wins and nothing is driven back into the host port. D2 also stops USB back-feeding the"
		(at 20.32 156.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "7fd7a61d-ec7f-4258-912a-4aea8e7cbb34")
	)
	(text "buck. Do not set the buck above ~5.3 V or it will push current into the host through D2."
		(at 20.32 159.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "38f608d5-e8bf-43c7-995b-3efb489fb4ad")
	)
	(text "3.  BATTERY SENSE  ->  GPIO8"
		(at 20.32 177.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.2 3.2)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d153ff35-f887-409d-b7b2-d1d8bb1be04b")
	)
	(text "Ratio (220+39)/39 = 6.641 - SENSOR_BATTERY_VOLTAGE_DIVIDER must match, and it takes a float."
		(at 20.32 248.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "8c224dd2-c665-44dc-859c-aa9ebaa40a78")
	)
	(text "15 V gives 2.26 V at the pin, inside the S2 ADC's 0..2500 mV linear range; 12.6 V gives 1.90 V."
		(at 20.32 251.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "13934b19-e059-49c0-8b7a-9d269634c8c7")
	)
	(text "High values because a 12 V bank moves slowly, so 49 uA of standing drain is worth more than"
		(at 20.32 254.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ec203e93-979a-4f0a-9764-931898a062fa")
	)
	(text "resolution. C4 is required, not optional: source impedance is 220k||39k = 33 k, far above the"
		(at 20.32 257.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "b34d857d-94c2-49d5-aaba-238cefee9531")
	)
	(text "ADC's 10 k preference, and tau = 3.3 ms against a 10 s sample interval."
		(at 20.32 260.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e474d5fc-bff4-42fe-8c8b-bd86db3fee26")
	)
	(text "With the lower leg fitted an absent 12 V rail reads ~0 mV rather than floating, which is why"
		(at 20.32 263.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c4c92a8a-242a-489a-bd0a-55bdb907bf54")
	)
	(text "SYSTEM_POWER_BAD_READING_MV=9000 is safe and the old \"comment it out on USB\" note is gone."
		(at 20.32 266.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a20fbcaa-2e89-4bf9-b7e0-0691dbd9fb6c")
	)
	(text "4.  TANK LEVEL  ->  GPIO6"
		(at 20.32 287.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.2 3.2)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0a9474bc-75bf-4cc9-987a-300c75eceba2")
	)
	(text "field wiring ->"
		(at 114.3 299.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.7 1.7)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d667b05d-7912-4130-b0a1-209929d85bc3")
	)
	(text "in the tank"
		(at 121.92 340.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.7 1.7)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "16f61e81-b3fd-4f82-becb-3f4c666e225e")
	)
	(text "R3 and the sender divide 3V3: 0R empty, 170R full -> 0.567 V full. An OPEN circuit pulls the"
		(at 20.32 358.14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "4ca54952-bcc9-4108-9cdc-a0a7ebc6e853")
	)
	(text "pin to 3V3, which the firmware reports as \"no sender fitted\" rather than as an empty tank -"
		(at 20.32 361.14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f6d40744-ba60-4c34-a741-280435b8d863")
	)
	(text "the distinction OSPIT could not make, and why a missing sender does not block irrigation."
		(at 20.32 364.14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "df8e8733-fa75-40c1-be55-44ef7f45cac3")
	)
	(text "The resistances are nominal and were never measured, so calibrate: Tare with the tank empty,"
		(at 20.32 367.14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "aa7f37cd-407f-437a-a7c4-cb73a38ae7a5")
	)
	(text "then enter 100 with it full. Run the sender on shielded or twisted cable."
		(at 20.32 370.14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ad503f5e-e9c9-4ea1-8bcf-f227d56453ed")
	)
	(text "5.  POWER FLAGS"
		(at 254 190.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.2 3.2)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "1289af25-f680-4983-b774-5317c83933ff")
	)
	(text "ERC only, no hardware. Each of these rails is sourced by a module pin, a"
		(at 254 231.14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "fdf8be56-1931-43b3-913e-5134593a7c0f")
	)
	(text "connector or a power symbol rather than by a regulator on this sheet, so"
		(at 254 234.14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e7c67ea3-bdd6-4e1f-aa62-8b8bdb8697c8")
	)
	(text "ERC needs telling that they really are driven."
		(at 254 237.14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "aaea12b1-c00c-418c-89ff-878b42d700ff")
	)
	(text "6.  CONTROLLER"
		(at 254 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.2 3.2)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "4818d1f3-c6fa-404e-b8d2-c424b2d6907c")
	)
	(text "Thirty-two pins on one part: drawn with net labels, which is how an MCU is normally shown."
		(at 254 147.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ea7bf74e-20d5-470c-9b69-914b9e77639f")
	)
	(text "The blocks that are real circuits - the input, the supply, the two dividers and each output"
		(at 254 150.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ede70b94-14b0-42d1-9fac-50bf4b9c4a54")
	)
	(text "channel - are drawn as circuits."
		(at 254 153.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c3e87bba-3505-4587-9ef9-05fb15b76021")
	)
	(text "Powered through VBUS (pin 25), never through the 3V3 pin: feeding 3V3 directly would"
		(at 254 159.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c79dfea3-287d-4887-a188-57a93a60a5f9")
	)
	(text "back-drive the module's own regulator. 12 V to 3.3 V with an LDO is not an option either -"
		(at 254 162.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "553e4aa8-f834-4ced-aa9e-f0f6888471a4")
	)
	(text "at the S2's ~300 mA WiFi peak that is (12-3.3) x 0.3 = 2.6 W, which needs a heatsink."
		(at 254 165.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "8f3f4f85-1640-4ffc-811f-062210546006")
	)
	(text "Unused GPIOs are marked no-connect. GPIO0/45/46 are the S2 strapping pins and none of the"
		(at 254 168.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "6d5876db-df61-4bf3-9684-d42abd343d32")
	)
	(text "pins used here are among them, so nothing here affects boot mode."
		(at 254 171.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "01768487-4b62-4a8f-b927-01930b1d54e3")
	)
	(text "7.  RS485 BUS AND SOIL PROBES"
		(at 457.2 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.2 3.2)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "7c0c9ba8-7136-49a8-a22a-26aa7607b184")
	)
	(text "THE MODULE MUST SWITCH DIRECTION ITSELF. The firmware defines no DE/RE pin, so"
		(at 457.2 248.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "722bbd52-98ac-4910-855f-6ef464e6abc2")
	)
	(text "System_RS485::txEnable() does nothing at all - a plain MAX485 breakout with a DE/RE jumper"
		(at 457.2 252.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a915817e-6868-4c12-8990-8ef66cba52bf")
	)
	(text "will receive but never transmit. Search for the words \"automatic flow control\"."
		(at 457.2 255.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "4f62c9cc-1da7-4cf1-9d5f-9919f44252b3")
	)
	(text "R14 (120R) belongs at the FAR END of the bus, at the last probe - not on this board. Fit"
		(at 457.2 261.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e6b33dca-929b-49be-8fa3-d224d8fa3e47")
	)
	(text "ONE termination only. With 120R at both ends the pair below gives just 3.3 x 60/1420 ="
		(at 457.2 264.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "b9e9c9a2-0b46-4ef5-aeef-49b021028f81")
	)
	(text "139 mV of idle differential, under the 200 mV the standard asks for; use 470R instead."
		(at 457.2 268.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "602c27b9-8bd3-4ee4-b145-dc4a621f4218")
	)
	(text "R15/R16 are fail-safe bias and are marked DNP because most auto-direction modules already"
		(at 457.2 274.52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "02a3b6ba-468e-4971-964b-d27da7987a9c")
	)
	(text "fit bias and termination. CHECK YOURS before adding a second set."
		(at 457.2 277.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "93a5264e-eb79-465e-8027-105b63b127d3")
	)
	(text "Probes accept 5-30 V so they run straight off the 12 V rail. Slave ids are auto-provisioned"
		(at 457.2 284.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ee83d861-08aa-45a5-a6da-45b5b60ee85b")
	)
	(text "from 2 upwards, so connect the probes ONE AT A TIME, in sector order - address 1 has to keep"
		(at 457.2 287.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "b500aadc-6c7c-4cd2-beca-f9d0017edb7e")
	)
	(text "meaning \"not yet provisioned\". Field cable: shielded twisted pair, one pair A/B and one pair"
		(at 457.2 290.52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "b4603685-d3ec-45bc-bcd9-66b5e87ed4a3")
	)
	(text "12 V/GND, shield earthed at the controller end only."
		(at 457.2 293.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "40976c62-29d2-42df-ae15-f3cc0d55239b")
	)
	(text "8.  OUTPUT DRIVERS  -  one block per channel.  Only GPIO, +12 V and GND leave a block;  the driver is on pages 2-6"
		(at 20.32 381 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.2 3.2)
